This November I got up early and read on a bench by the lake. Counting how many pages I could read while the mist lifted became a small game.

## This month's five

1. **Jane Eyre**: the red room chapter still gets me every time ★★★★★
2. **Pride and Prejudice**: I forgot how fast the dialogue is ★★★★☆
3. **Hamlet**: one short soliloquy, a whole day of thinking ★★★★☆
4. **The Velveteen Rabbit**: read it aloud and it becomes a different book ★★★★★
5. **Don Quixote**: halfway. I have reached the windmills ★★★☆☆

> Reading is not about finishing fast. It is about what stays.

All five are on the sample shelf of the NanumOS Books app, ready to read.
